  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Costa Rica, a sustainable model for combination prevention and care for the MSM and female transgendered population - Costa Rica (01-Jul-2015-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Costa Rica, HIV, Humanist Institute for Co-operation with Developing Countries (Hivos) (HIVOS -  HubLA)This program has the following goals: Ensure universal access to prevention, treatment and HIV care  service for MSM and female transgenders under the implementation area..  Reduce AIDS related mortality to 2.5 per 100,000. The objectives of this program are: Ensure universal access to prevention, treatment and HIV care services for MSM and female transgender under the implmentation area.  Improve country level HIV strategic information on key populations to facilitate decision making.  Improve the legal, social and poiliticla environment for hte full excercise of human rights among MSM and transger popupluations, including people living with HIV</narrative>
  </description>
